[Verse 1]
I drew a door in chalk
And it opened slow for me
I sketched a sky in ink
And watched it turn to sea

A box of scraps, a spark
A map across the floor
I touched the broken edge
And made it into more

[Pre-Chorus]
If it lives inside your head
It can live outside
Hold the smallest flame
Watch it learn to ride

[Chorus]
You can make it real
You can make it real
From the quiet spark
To the tallest wheel

You can make it real
You can make it real
What you cannot see
You can shape and feel

[Verse 2]
I built a bridge from thread
Crossed every hidden doubt
I stitched a golden path
Where there was only out

A room with no windows
Now it’s wide with dawn
A song that had no name
Now everybody sings along

[Pre-Chorus]
If it lives inside your chest
Let it take the light
Give it breath, give it bones
Let it rise tonight

[Chorus]
You can make it real
You can make it real
From the quiet spark
To the tallest wheel

You can make it real
You can make it real
What you cannot see
You can shape and feel

[Bridge]
Hold on to the image
Even if it shakes
Every crown begins
As paper in your hands

Call it, then believe it
Let the future wake
You were born to build
With a little fire and sand

[Final Chorus]
You can make it real
You can make it real
From the quiet spark
To the tallest wheel

You can make it real
You can make it real
What you cannot see
You can shape and feel

You can make it real
You can make it real
Lift it in the dark
And watch it fill the sky